🚽 Test case: regression for #206 (3a) -- compute_struct_layout()/
🚽 compute_union_layout() must produce C-ABI-honest alignment and trailing
🚽 padding, not a packed layout. Every size below is what a real C
🚽 compiler produces for the equivalent struct/union; before this fix they
🚽 were all under-sized because fields were packed back-to-back with no
🚽 alignment rounding. tests/abi/struct_layout_abi_check.c independently
🚽 establishes, via _Static_assert/offsetof against real C struct
🚽 declarations, that these are the sizes/offsets a real C compiler
🚽 produces for the same field lists -- it does NOT touch Brainrot's own
🚽 layout code, so it is ground truth for what the numbers below should
🚽 be, not proof that Brainrot's computed layout matches them.
🚽
🚽 maxxing() alone only proves total size: a struct that packed `n` right
🚽 after `flag` with no interior padding, then padded the *total* up to
🚽 16 at the very end, would also report 16 here despite `n` being at the
🚽 wrong offset. main() below writes a distinct value into every field of
🚽 Mixed and reads them all back: if any pair of fields' true offsets
🚽 OVERLAPPED, one write would corrupt a value already written by another
🚽 and the read-back would disagree with what was stored. That catches
🚽 an overlap, not every wrong offset: a regression that mis-aligned `n`
🚽 to 1 instead of 4 (`n` at [1,5), `flag` at [0,1), `d` still correctly
🚽 8-aligned since its own alignment doesn't depend on `n`'s) produces
🚽 non-overlapping ranges AND the same total 16 -- Mixed's own trailing
🚽 double masks a wrong int alignment from both checks this file runs on
🚽 it. CharInt below exists specifically to catch that: with no
🚽 larger-alignment field after it to force the same total regardless,
🚽 a wrong int alignment changes CharInt's total size outright.
gang Mixed {
    cap flag;    🚽 bool,   1 byte,  align 1 -> offset 0
    rizz n;      🚽 int,    4 bytes, align 4 -> offset 4 (3 bytes padding)
    gigachad d;  🚽 double, 8 bytes, align 8 -> offset 8 (4 bytes padding)
};               🚽 total: 16 (offset 8 + 8, already 8-aligned)

gang Triple {
    rizz a;
    rizz b;
    rizz c;
};               🚽 total: 12, align 4 -- no padding needed here

chungus WideUnion {
    gang Triple t; 🚽 size 12, align 4
    gigachad d;    🚽 size 8,  align 8
};                 🚽 max member size 12 rounded up to max align 8 -> 16

gang CharInt {
    yap a;  🚽 char, 1 byte, align 1 -> offset 0
    rizz b; 🚽 int,  4 bytes, align 4 -> offset 4 (3 bytes padding)
};          🚽 total: 8. If get_struct_field_alignment(VAR_INT) ever
            🚽 regressed to align 1, b would land at offset 1 and the
            🚽 struct would total 5, not 8 -- unlike Mixed, nothing
            🚽 bigger-aligned follows to force the same total anyway.

skibidi main {
    gang Mixed m;
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(m));

    m.flag = W;
    m.n = 1234567;
    m.d = 2.5;
    yapping("%b", m.flag);   🚽 would print corrupted garbage if n/d
    yapping("%d", m.n);      🚽 overlapped flag/each other instead of
    yapping("%f", m.d);      🚽 landing at their C-correct offsets

    chungus WideUnion u;
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(u));

    gang CharInt ci;
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(ci));
}
